.TH TULPAR-INFO 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.5.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-info, tulpar-show \- show full metadata for a package
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar info
.RI [ options "] " "name|file.apg"
.br
.B tulpar show
.RI [ options "] " name
.br
.B tulpar n
.RI [ options "] " name
.br
.B tulpar \-n
.RI [ options "] " name
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows full metadata for
.IR name ,
including dependencies, provides, conflicts, replaces, and reverse
dependencies (Required By) for locally installed packages.
The local package database is checked first; if the package is not
installed, the configured repositories are queried instead.
.B info
and
.B show
are equivalent spellings of the same command.
.PP
When the argument is the path of an existing
.B .apg
file, the metadata is read from that archive instead, and the status line
says whether a package of the same name is installed. Nothing is
extracted or installed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Look up in the local database of an alternate root.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print the metadata as a JSON object instead of human-readable text. See
.BR tulpar-json (7).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if the package was found, non-zero otherwise.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-search (1),
.BR tulpar-list (1)
